1. NTO Sandpiper
   https://github.com/National-Tutoring-Observatory/sandpiper
   Commit b437988 (2026-09-08)

   Two files are copied into this repository:
   vendor/sandpiper/getKappaInterpretation.ts
     <- app/modules/evaluations/helpers/getKappaInterpretation.ts
        Copied unchanged, below a six-line origin header. Zero imports. It
        implements the Landis & Koch bands and is the source of this project's
        AGREEMENT_THRESHOLD = 0.61. See docs/DEVIATIONS.md D-010.
   vendor/sandpiper/calculateCohensKappa.ts
     <- app/modules/evaluations/helpers/calculateCohensKappa.ts
        Copied unchanged, below a six-line origin header. Zero imports. It
        computes Cohen's kappa between two equal-length, positionally aligned
        label sequences; this project calls it on one annotation run and one
        LLM run, at the turn level. Its two upstream edge cases are left as
        found: it returns 1 when expected agreement is 1, so two runs that
        annotate nothing score a perfect 1, and it returns 0 on a length
        mismatch rather than raising. Refusing those two inputs is the job of
        a thin wrapper [OURS: an edited vendored file is no longer
        attributable, so the refusals live outside the copy]. See
        docs/DEVIATIONS.md.

   Nothing else is copied. An earlier draft forked Sandpiper's
   app/lib/schemas/json/transcript.schema.json; that fork was abandoned on
   2026-09-17 and the transcript shape is this project's own. Two things are
   taken as design rather than as code, and neither carries copied text: the
   codebook structure, and the turn-level transcript field names. See
   docs/SPEC-gate0.md §10.

